# TODO - Native Linux packaging

## Objective

Produce portable Linux x86-64 executables with local asset discovery.

## Acceptance

- Do not link or bundle original game executables or libraries.
- Verify startup, save paths, packaging and Linux gameplay smoke tests.

## Evidence

The selected-title release build produced an 835,768-byte dynamically
linked x86-64 ELF executable on the development host. Its direct dynamic
dependencies were SDL2, libgcc and libc; it does not use the original game
executable or library. The hidden native four-player movement smoke passed
with four verified local art bundles. This verifies local startup, not
portable distribution, independent asset discovery, saves or complete
gameplay. Those remain open.
